---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import ExperimentStatus from '../../components/ExperimentStatus.astro';
import MetricTable from '../../components/MetricTable.astro';
import QualitativeSamples from '../../components/QualitativeSamples.astro';
import SpectralExplorer from '../../components/SpectralExplorer.astro';
import TrajectoryExplorer from '../../components/TrajectoryExplorer.astro';
import Caveats from '../../components/Caveats.astro';
import NextExperiments from '../../components/NextExperiments.astro';
import { projects } from '../../data/projects';
import type { Project } from '../../types';
import { withBase } from '../../utils/paths';

export function getStaticPaths() {
  return projects.map((project) => ({ params: { slug: project.slug }, props: { project } }));
}

interface Props { project: Project; }
const { project } = Astro.props;
const heroFigure = project.figures.find((figure) => figure.src.includes('ffhq128_mid_x0'))!;
---
<Base title={project.title + ' | Research projects'} description={project.contribution}>
  <article>
    <header class="project-hero shell">
      <div class="hero-meta"><span>Streaming trajectory report</span><span>Image generation · decoded intermediate states</span></div>
      <div class="hero-grid">
        <div class="hero-intro"><h1>{project.title}</h1><p class="hero-subtitle">When does an intermediate image become a useful preview?</p></div>
        <div class="hero-result" aria-label="Scope of the trajectory audit">
          <p class="result-context">Completed checkpoint audit <span>·</span> DCTdiff, FAR and released comparators</p>
          <div class="hero-metric"><strong>21</strong><span>sampled<br />public runs</span></div>
          <p class="hero-criterion"><span class="criterion-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>Plus ours A1 in the same views</p>
          <p class="hero-result-source">Eight samples per trajectory. A1 comes from a separate saved FFHQ-64 evaluation; read its quantitative findings in the dedicated report.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-deck"><p class="hero-contribution">{project.contribution}</p><a class="text-link" href="#visuals">Inspect the trajectories <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div>
      </div>
      <figure class="hero-figure"><a href={withBase(heroFigure.src)} target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Open full DCTdiff trajectory figure"><img src={withBase(heroFigure.src)} alt={heroFigure.alt} fetchpriority="high" /></a><figcaption><span>Reference trajectory / DCTdiff</span><span>{heroFigure.caption}</span></figcaption></figure>
    </header>

    <div class="shell story-grid">
      <aside class="story-nav" aria-label="On this page">
        <span class="nav-label">On this page</span>
        <a href="#question">The question</a>
        <a href="#visuals">Visual evidence</a>
        <a href="#instruments">Progression and graphs</a>
        <a href="#interpretation">What the audit shows</a>
        <a href="#status">Evidence and limits</a>
      </aside>

      <div class="story-content">
        <section id="question" class="story-section question-section">
          <p class="section-overline">The question</p>
          <h2>Seeing a state is not the same as seeing an image.</h2>
          <p class="section-lead">{project.question}</p>
          <div class="question-columns"><div><h3>Why it matters</h3><p>{project.motivation}</p></div><div><h3>What is measured</h3><p>Each decoded image is compared with its own final sample, frequency band by frequency band. This measures when a sample becomes decided, not realism against the dataset.</p></div></div>
        </section>

        <section id="visuals" class="story-section visuals-section">
          <div class="section-heading-row"><p class="section-overline">Generation progression</p><span class="evidence-tag">Eight samples per run</span></div>
          <h2>Watch the image take shape.</h2>
          <p class="section-lead">The same figure rail now includes our A1 cumulative FFHQ-64 stages alongside DCTdiff, FAR, D-AR, FlexVAR, VAR and DetailFlow. Each strip follows fixed samples across generation. Datasets, resolutions and samplers differ.</p>
          <QualitativeSamples findings={project.qualitative} figures={project.figures} />
          <a class="text-link" href={withBase('projects/next-frequency/')}>Read our separate A1 method and results report <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </section>

        <section id="instruments" class="story-section instruments-section">
          <div class="section-heading-row"><p class="section-overline">Interactive audit instruments</p><span class="evidence-tag">Official checkpoints + ours A1</span></div>
          <h2>Compare what appears, and when.</h2>
          <p class="section-lead">A1 appears as a row in the frequency settling graph, a curve panel, and a selectable four-stage strip in the trajectory viewer. Its measurements use the same luma FFT residual definition on its saved stage images.</p>
          <SpectralExplorer />
          <TrajectoryExplorer />
          <a class="text-link" href={withBase('report/')}>Read the original checkpoint audit and methods <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </section>

        <section id="interpretation" class="story-section interpretation-section">
          <p class="section-overline">What the trajectories show</p>
          <h2>Different routes to a preview.</h2>
          <p class="section-lead">{project.verdict}</p>
          <div class="interpretation-body"><p>{project.interpretation}</p><p>Our A1 stage sheet adds an explicitly ordered frequency path. The chart places its decoded stages on the same normalized progress axis; its four steps and FFHQ-64 data make that comparison descriptive rather than a controlled quality ranking.</p></div>
          <MetricTable rows={project.results} />
          <details class="technical-detail"><summary>Published ImageNet-256 methods in the report <span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>These paper and checkpoint FID figures are cited, not re-measured under a controlled ranking.</p><MetricTable rows={project.relatedMethods} /></details>
        </section>

        <section id="status" class="story-section status-section">
          <p class="section-overline">Evidence and limits</p>
          <h2>What is established here.</h2>
          <div class="status-rows"><div><ExperimentStatus status="completed" /><p>The 21 public-checkpoint trajectories and the original DCTdiff/FAR spectral audit are complete.</p></div><div><ExperimentStatus status="completed" /><p>Our A1 FFHQ-64 four-stage preview and matching spectral row are derived from eight saved 146k images.</p></div><div><ExperimentStatus status="reported" /><p>FID values belong to their source runs or papers. This report does not re-evaluate them under a common protocol; the separate A1 report gives its matched comparisons.</p></div></div>
          <details class="technical-detail audit-caveats"><summary>Limits of the trajectory comparison <span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><Caveats items={project.caveats} /></details>
        </section>

        <section id="next" class="story-section next-section">
          <p class="section-overline">Next experiment</p>
          <h2>Test previews under one protocol.</h2>
          <p class="section-lead">Compare trajectories on a shared dataset and sampling budget before ranking methods by preview quality or FID.</p>
          <details class="technical-detail"><summary>Other checks suggested by the audit <span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><NextExperiments items={project.nextExperiments} /></details>
          <div class="end-note"><span>Source boundary</span><p>{project.sourceNote} The A1 matched-run results and caveats live in <a href={withBase('projects/next-frequency/')}>the dedicated report</a>.</p><a class="text-link" href={withBase('report/')}>Read the original source report <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
